# intro-prologue-v3 — opening prologue cutscene, v3 drawcall/flow-parity window.
#
# New game → 1st HOUSE_FREEROAM (= the prologue cutscene start: load-overlay
# drop, still mid-iv1_1 conversation, per anchor_trace.c ev_house_freeroam /
# FREEROAM_START contrast). The intro-video load-stretch is BEFORE the anchor,
# so the offset-relative cutscene frames after it are deterministic; the first
# ~200 frames are line 1 of iv1_1 revealing + settling (NO advance input, so the
# typewriter plays naturally and the cutscene stays ON SCREEN the whole window —
# no mid-cutscene iv1_1->iv1_2 load seam this early).
#
# Head: spam C (0x10) frames 12..120 to drive title -> NEW game -> into the
# prologue (same head as intro-dialogue-lines). Then wait HOUSE_FREEROAM, pin
# phase+RNG at offset 0, caprange+calltrace [0,200].
#
# Drive (v3): nix develop --command python3 tools/trace_studio_v3/orv3_window.py \
#   intro-prologue-v3 --window 0:200 --anchor HOUSE_FREEROAM --max-frames 16000 \
#   --state --launch
